\label{assume: smoothness of g_0}
    For some $\beta>0$ and $L<\infty$,
    $$\int_{\mathbb{R}^d} (1 + \|t\|^2)^{\beta} |\varphi_{g_0}(t)|^2 dt \leq L^2.$$

\label{assume: kernel}
    The kernel $K:\mathbb{R}^d\to \mathbb{R}$ is integrable, belongs to $C^3\cap L^2$, and satisfies $\int_{\mathbb{R}^d} K(u) du = 1$. It is spherically symmetric:
    $$K(Qu) = K(u) \qquad \text{for every } u\in \mathbb{R}^d, \; Q\in \mathcal{O}(d).$$
    In addition:

