    $$A^+ - B^+ = -A^+ E B^+ + A^+(A^+)^\top E^\top (I-BB^+) + (I-A^+A)E^\top (B^+)^\top B^+.$$

First, insert the identities $I=BB^+ + (I-BB^+)$ and $I=A^+A + (I-A^+A)$ to split:
    $$A^+-B^+ = \underbrace{A^+(I-BB^+)}_{\text{term 1}} - \underbrace{(I-A^+A)B^+}_{\text{term 2}} - \underbrace{A^+(A-B)B^+}_{=A^+EB^+}.$$
    The last term is already in the target form. We focus on the first two terms.

    Recall the fundamental property of pseudo-inverse $A^+=A^+(A^+)^\top A^\top$. Plugging this into term 1 gives
    $$A^+(I-BB^+) = A^+(A^+)^\top A^\top (I-BB^+).$$
