    and $a>0$ is a sufficiently small constant. By the moment conditions on $\psi$, $\int g_\theta = 1$, $\mathbb{E}_{g_\theta}[X]=0$ and $\mathbb{E}_{g_\theta}[XX^\top]=I_d$. Since all perturbations are supported on the fixed compact cube $K$ and $g_*$ is bounded away from 0 on $K$, choosing $a$ sufficiently small guarantees $g_\theta \geq 0$. The Gaussian-tail is also preserved as the perturbation vanishes outside $K$. Finally, standard scaling of Sobolev norms give $\|\sum_j \theta_j \psi_{j,h}\|_{\mathcal{W}_\beta}^2 \lesssim M h^{d-2\beta}$. Since $M\asymp h^{-d}$, we get $\|\epsilon_h \sum_j \theta_j \psi_{j,h}\|_{\mathcal{W}_\beta} \lesssim \epsilon_h h^{-\beta} \leq a$. Because $g_*$ is in the interior, $a$ can be chosen sufficiently small so that $g_\theta\in \mathcal{G}_\beta(L,C)$ for every $\theta$.

    \medskip
    \noindent
    \textbf{Separation} Let $r_D=\frac{1}{\sqrt{D}h}$.  By scaling 
    $$\|\psi_{j,h}\star \phi_{D^{-1}I_d} - \psi_{j,h}\|_{L^1} = h^d \|\psi \star \phi_{r_D^2 I_d} - \psi\|_{L^1}.$$
    Since $\|\psi\star \phi_{r^2 I_d} - \psi\|_{L^1} \to 0$  as $r \to 0$, there is a constant $r_0>0$ such that whenever $r_D\leq r_0$, $\|\psi\star \phi_{r_D^2 I_d} - \psi\|_{L^1} \leq \frac12 \|\psi\|_{L^1}$.

    Let $\theta,\theta'\in \{-1,1\}^M$. Write $q_{\theta,D}=q_{g_\theta, D}$. Since 
    $$q_{\theta,D} - q_{\theta',D} = \epsilon_h \sum_{j=1}^M (\theta_j - \theta_j') \psi_{j,h} \star \phi_{D^{-1}I_d},$$
